{
  "comment": [
    "Partner-API model families and the variants each one offers, read by both packages",
    "the way seedanceVersions.json is: backend/src/partnerModels.ts (which lets a variant",
    "override what workflowService would otherwise infer from the file name, prices it, and",
    "maps its resolutions onto node values) and src/features/generation/partnerModels.ts",
    "(which groups the variants under one Workflow card with a Model version picker).",
    "",
    "One variant is one workflow file under workflow/, named by `modelId` -- the slug",
    "workflowService derives from the file name. The file carries the node and its model",
    "value; this table carries what the file cannot say: the artist-facing label and hint,",
    "the limits the node enforces, and the price. Adding a model version is therefore one",
    "exported graph plus one row here. A variant with no capability fields keeps whatever",
    "the existing inference gives it, which is how GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana 2 join a",
    "family without their behaviour changing.",
    "",
    "Every limit and price below is transcribed from the ComfyUI 0.38.0 partner nodes the",
    "Animation worker (mkxh60tw6we1t0) runs: nodes_openai.py, nodes_gemini.py,",
    "nodes_bytedance.py, nodes_minimax.py and apis/bytedance.py. Prices are the nodes' own",
    "price-badge rates in USD. The credit tracker records the real charge from the proxy's",
    "X-Comfy-Credits-Used header after the run; these only drive the estimate shown before it.",
    "",
    "resolutions[].value is what the picker sends as resolution.label; nodeValue is what the",
    "node's `resolution` combo takes (MiniMax spells 768P with a capital P); sizePreset is",
    "Seedream's `size_preset` label, and matchInput sizes a Custom request to the first",
    "input image's aspect at width*height pixels.",
    "",
    "pricing: perImageUsd and perSecondUsd are keyed by resolution value, with \"*\" as the",
    "fallback. perReferenceImageUsd is added per input image. maxExtraUsd is an upper bound",
    "added for reference videos, whose charge depends on the clip and cannot be known before",
    "the run, so the estimate leans high rather than surprising anyone.",
    "",
    "draft.kind names a Draft -> Final flow in draftFinal.ts. A MiniMax H3 768P render is a",
    "draft its Regenerate node can re-render at 2K; draft.resolution says which output counts."
  ],
